# 7. Hard dependency graph

The original dependency relationships remain valid unless fresh source disproves them:

```text
BUG-OBSERVE-01
    └── BUG-KEYWORD-01
        shared authoritative SourceSnapshot contract

BUG-METADATA-02
    └── BUG-METADATA-01
        identity validation before metadata mutation

BUG-DATE-01
    └── BUG-DATE-02
        typed lookup outcome before child/parent terminal semantics

BUG-HISTORY-01
    └── BUG-KEYWORD-02
        atomic HistoryUndoSnapshot before RULE recomputation

BUG-BACKUP-04
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-05
    └── BUG-BACKUP-07
        typed/consistent capture boundary before payload extensions

BUG-BACKUP-03 requires the applicable backup/restore prerequisites:
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-01 semantic closure, including Finding B where relevant
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-04
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-02
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-06
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-08
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-05
    ├── BUG-BACKUP-07
    └── BUG-CLEANUP-01
```

Additional sequencing rules from current remediation:

```text
BUG-OUTPUT-01 independent CLEAN
    └── Finding B may begin

Finding B independent CLEAN
    └── full current-source F1 / BUG-BACKUP-01 re-review and closure
        └── downstream backup/restore defects may rely on BUG-BACKUP-01 closure

Crash evidence preservation
    └── MainActivity startup/lifecycle root-cause correction

Link input/share extraction
    └── canonical source/media identity should consume the normalized input contract

canonical source/media identity
    └── History duplicate/destructive logic should use explicit identity rather than titles or URL spelling
```

An independent-review gate blocks only defects that depend on it. Unrelated defects may be implemented while the gate is pending, but no dependent defect may treat `CANDIDATE_COMPLETE` or self-review PASS as equivalent to independent CLEAN.

The last three are preferred sequencing/contract dependencies and must be validated against current source before being treated as hard schema dependencies.

